From ad84f1348271bfc077d7e83845eeb3bdc1394669 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JingMatrix <jingmatrix@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 22:51:06 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 21/47] Mint target apps' attest keys in the TA, routed by
 caller uid

An app creating an attestation key (ATTEST_KEY purpose) does so unattested: no
challenge and no application id, so ProfileForRequest's name match cannot see it.
Match the caller's uid as a fallback (profiles now carry their resolved uids) so
such a request is still routed to the app's profile. At the AIBinder_transact
hook the calling identity is still the app's, so AIBinder_getCallingUid is the
real app uid.

Handle an ATTEST_KEY-purpose creation before the attest-key branch and always
mint it in the TA (generation, forwarding std::nullopt), ignoring any attest key
keystore2 injected to attest it. On TrustedEnvironment, attesting a new attest
key that carries a challenge makes keystore2 inject a remote-provisioned real
hardware key, which would otherwise be seen as a foreign attest key and forwarded
- leaving us an attest key we can never re-root. We must hold this key's private
key so the leaves it later signs get a patched root of trust. StrongBox has no
such injection, which is why StrongBox already worked and TE did not.

For a leaf that carries an attest key, keystore2 appends that attest key's own
stored chain, so emit only the leaf: sign it in the TA when the attest key is
ours, otherwise forward to the real HAL. Drop the OverrideAttestKey path and its
replacement-key cache entirely - a minted replacement A' collided with keystore2's
own appended real attest cert (same subject, different key) and broke the chain;
the durable fix is that attest keys are now ours. Also log every generateKey and
each key-blob operation (begin/delete/upgrade/getKeyCharacteristics) with whether
the blob is ours.
---
 keymint/keymint_router.cpp | 124 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 107 insertions(+), 17 deletions(-)

diff --git a/keymint/keymint_router.cpp b/keymint/keymint_router.cpp
